  "problem": "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n${cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{5\\pi }{12})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{5\\pi }{12})=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{5\\pi }{12})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}) & =cos\\,(2\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =cos\\,(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
